runtime: bound SSH discovery and isolate runner sessions

Wait for each recorded SSH endpoint under the existing readiness deadline,
retain bounded native diagnostics privately, and publish initial trust only
when every machine succeeds. Retained host-key trust and strict guest
identity checks remain unchanged.

Establish the runner's own POSIX session before creating machines while
preserving its PID, argument vector, receipt and cleanup authority. This
separates inherited terminal/group lifetime without escaping cgroup policy
or changing the retained predecessor.
